Desktop app (src-tauri), additionally:

- Tauri and its plugins localhost and dialog (https://tauri.app)
  Copyright (c) 2019-2026 Tauri Programme within The Commons Conservancy. MIT or Apache-2.0.
  The desktop binaries also contain Rust crates under MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, Zlib and
  Unicode licences, and a few unmodified MPL-2.0 crates (cssparser, selectors, dtoa-short,
  option-ext; source on crates.io). The full list is in src-tauri/Cargo.lock.
  The Linux AppImage includes WebKitGTK and GTK (LGPL-2.1), dynamically linked and unmodified;
  the .deb / .rpm packages use the system's copies.

Tools invoked as separate programs (not distributed with Axion):

- arduino-cli (https://github.com/arduino/arduino-cli), GPL-3.0.
  Axion calls it as an external process to compile sketches locally.

Prebuilt example firmware:

- The .hex files in examples/ and the boards' template.hex starter firmware were
  compiled from the Arduino AVR core and its Wire, SPI and Servo libraries
  (https://github.com/arduino), LGPL-2.1. Their sources are available from those
  projects; each example's sketch.ino sits next to its .hex file.
- The Raspberry Pi Pico .hex files (examples/pico-*, src/parts/pi-pico/template.hex) were
  compiled with the arduino-pico core 6.3.1 (https://github.com/earlephilhower/arduino-pico,
  LGPL-2.1), which includes the Pico SDK (BSD 3-Clause) and TinyUSB (MIT).
